{"title":"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Alternative_Ending_to_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Alternative Ending to Solution 1</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Clever_way_using_divisibility_rules)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Clever way using divisibility rules)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/5/52503385edca4db0f227ae98c9ac42205b28420a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=123456789101112\\dots4344$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"240\" height=\"13\" /> be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/8/cd8b908d15627ea3a118bb38668d865edf722170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$79$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-digit number that is formed by writing the integers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b45828f292e161290be6ee62bc4c9df081ee1e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> in order, one after the other. What is the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1929e41961587ee09272908be642ced7896db86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 4\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 9\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 18\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"367\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We only need to find the remainders of N when divided by 5 and 9 to determine the answer.\nBy inspection, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c441a9cd2148d28626c82d200731db6ff84aee06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N \\equiv 4 \\text{ (mod 5)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"17\" />.\nThe remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/8/d084a6545289c869d6a27851a2dc21b62cb2f9de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2+3+4+ \\cdots +1+0+1+1 +1+2 +\\cdots + 4+3+4+4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"503\" height=\"14\" />, but since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caa90f5312e130b7091692ce9bb9f04f7918ed4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\equiv 1 \\text{ (mod 9)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"17\" />, we can also write this as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/4/8547beb45ee8db0be6880569ebec074f36fddca0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2+3 +\\cdots +10+11+12+ \\cdots 43 + 44 = \\frac{44 \\cdot 45}2 = 22 \\cdot 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"492\" height=\"37\" />, which has a remainder of 0 mod 9. Solving these modular congruence using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chinese_Remainder_Theorem\" title=\"Chinese Remainder Theorem\">Chinese Remainder Theorem</a> we get the remainder to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/6/45631acc3fceaf75f264c9f83ca05f38d0c35eb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\pmod{45}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/5/1d52c42c934344fefe4d51b4221fd7acaf0f7e6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Alternative_Ending_to_Solution_1\">Alternative Ending to Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Alternative Ending to Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Once we find our 2 modular congruences, we can narrow our options down to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/1/1716e238f553f7dabd85afad448d78d505bc0ce1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${C}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/9/b29f5f47e0eda4a96ade3c908bda26c59faa83fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${D}$\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" /> because the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> should be a multiple of 9 by our modular congruence that states <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> has a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Also, our other modular congruence states that the remainder when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> should have a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Out of options <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/5/1d52c42c934344fefe4d51b4221fd7acaf0f7e6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" /> satisfies that the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5eee9393438304d48b26aea020a0580c48f24765.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45 \\equiv 4 \\text{ (mod 5)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/a/fca9d906bf9deebdb84cb73f4f6c9c4ca7bbee24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\equiv 10 \\cdot 10 \\equiv 10^{k} \\pmod{45}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"222\" height=\"20\" /> for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Apply this on the expanded form of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/5/b8524fd0d2710676fb631c3c3f312138350881ed.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N = 1(10)^{78} + 2(10)^{77} + \\cdots + 9(10)^{70} + 10(10)^{68} + 11(10)^{66} + \\cdots + 43(10)^{2} + 44 \\equiv\\]\" width=\"586\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/0/d203a7381751235f0e090751113e1dbebd45b293.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10(1 + 2 + \\cdots + 43) + 44 \\equiv 10 \\left (\\frac{43 \\cdot 44}2 \\right ) + 44 \\equiv\\]\" width=\"379\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/0924e40261af25ef52f841ecbceab37c6831aa00.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10 \\left (\\frac{-2 \\cdot -1}2 \\right ) - 1 \\equiv \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 9} \\pmod{45}\\]\" width=\"310\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Clever_way_using_divisibility_rules.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Clever_way_using_divisibility_rules)\">Solution 3 (Clever way using divisibility rules)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Clever way using divisibility rules)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/3/89326b24e14bdb40eaa392136cdfe410dae39f55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45 = 5 \\cdot 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" />, so we can apply our restrictions to that. We know that the units digit must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the digits must add up to a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c439f58430dde7f6758b0802829d2d3360f14ff3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2+3+4+\\cdots + 44 = \\frac{44 \\cdot 45}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"266\" height=\"38\" />. We can quickly see this is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/c/3dc1618e6803169ed76886ce002c446d94597e3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{44}{2} \\cdot 45 = 22 \\cdot 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"129\" height=\"38\" />. We know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/7/997dd9eba877392ca6c7a0e9e68a37f09d8b3f1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$123 \\ldots 4344$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"14\" /> is not a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because the units digit isn't <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We can just subtract by 9 until we get a number whose units digit is 5 or 0.\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/7/997dd9eba877392ca6c7a0e9e68a37f09d8b3f1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$123 \\ldots 4344$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we can subtract by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/0/fe0c9390a51f00f43aef6a3b7534636c83011781.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$123 \\ldots 4335$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"14\" /> and we know that this is divisible by 5. So our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/5/1d52c42c934344fefe4d51b4221fd7acaf0f7e6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~Arcticturn\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> ends with the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/4/ca4a370623a14ae3f239c99c5b3e94ba48329a3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N\\equiv 4\\pmod 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" />. Also, the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> are divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, we have the system of equations:\n</p>\n<pre><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/4/ca4a370623a14ae3f239c99c5b3e94ba48329a3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N\\equiv 4\\pmod 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/1/c8188bf89c2a8b3a9231ca71fca6bd6a059a917b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N\\equiv 0\\pmod 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" />\n</pre>\n<p>According to the second equation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e0899b05793d75a4130d1c5acae5e0a013493f9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N\\equiv \\{0, 9, 18, 27, 36\\} \\pmod {45}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"247\" height=\"20\" />. The only one of these solutions that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/3/ca3134f6454c0019fe092b526efd5982ab4ef6ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\pmod 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/5/1d52c42c934344fefe4d51b4221fd7acaf0f7e6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />\n~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Sid2012\">sid2012</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B\">2017 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 